Jackson, and Elizabeth Peña.

15
00:59:28,965 --> 00:59:34,965
Set in a retro-futuristic version of the 1960s, the film follows Bob and
Helen Parr, a superhero couple respectively known as Mr.

16
01:03:26,896 --> 01:03:32,896
Incredible and Elastigirl, who hide their powers in accordance with a government mandate that
outlawed superheroes, and attempt to live a quiet suburban life with their three children.

17
01:07:24,827 --> 01:07:30,827
However, Bob's desire to help people draws the entire family into
a confrontation with a vengeful fan-turned-foe.

18
01:11:22,758 --> 01:11:28,758
Bird, who was Pixar's first outside director, developed the film as an extension of the
1960s comic books and spy films from his boyhood and personal family life.

19
01:15:20,689 --> 01:15:26,689
He pitched the film to Pixar after Warner Bros.' box office disappointment of his first feature, The
Iron Giant (1999), and carried over much of its staff to develop The Incredibles.

20
01:19:18,620 --> 01:19:24,620
The animation team was tasked with animating an all-human cast, which required creating new
technology to animate detailed human anatomy, clothing, and realistic skin and hair.

21
01:23:16,551 --> 01:23:22,551
Michael Giacchino composed the film's orchestral score.

22
01:27:14,482 --> 01:27:20,482
The Incredibles debuted at the El Capitan Theatre on October 24, 2004, and
was released in theaters in the United States on November 5.

23
01:31:12,413 --> 01:31:18,413
It earned $632 million worldwide, finishing its theatrical run
as the fourth-highest-grossing film of 2004.

24
01:35:10,344 --> 01:35:16,344
The Incredibles received widespread acclaim from critics, with praise for its animation,
screenplay, voice acting, action sequences, sound design, humor, and music.

25
01:39:08,275 --> 01:39:14,275
The film won Best Animated Feature and Best Sound Editing at the 77th Academy Awards, with two additional nominations
for Best Original Screenplay and Best Sound Mixing, as well as the Annie Award for Best Animated Feature.

26
01:43:06,206 --> 01:43:12,206
It was the first entirely animated film to win the Hugo
Award for Best Dramatic Presentation.

27
01:47:04,137 --> 01:47:10,137
A sequel, Incredibles 2, was released in June 2018,
while a third film is in development.

28
01:51:02,068 --> 01:51:08,068
The film explores themes of hero, secret identity,
superhero, villain, family relationships.
